        {
          "id": "SP_OTOTYPHLONEMERTES_LONGISSIMA_LIU_SUN_2018",
          "name": "Ototyphlonemertes longissima Liu & Sun, 2018",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Ototyphlonemertes",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Body wall and musculature. The ciliated glandular epidermis is mostly about 10 – 20 µm thick. The dermis is about 1 – 2 µm thick. The body wall musculature consists of an outer circular and an inner longitudinal muscle layers, which are about 1 – 2 µm and 5 – 30 µm thick, respectively (Fig. 2 E). Proboscis apparatus. The rhynchodaeum opens ventrally near the anterior tip. It is lined by a thin epithelium without glands or cilia. The rhynchocoel accounts for about 1 / 8 of the body length, contains an outer circular and an inner longitudinal muscle layers. The anterior chamber of proboscis is about 3 – 6 mm long. The diaphragm is bulbous, about 160 – 230 µm in length. The middle chamber is tubular, 400 – 500 µm long (Fig. 1 D). The posterior chamber is 4 - 8 mm in length. The central stylet, which is 54 – 60 µm long, is composed of three twined strands. The stylet basis is cylindrical, and measures 50 – 52 µm long and 12 µm wide (Fig. 1 E). The ratio of stylet / basis is 1.06 – 1.17. Two accessory stylet pouches are situated lateral to the central stylet, each contains 4 – 6 accessory stylets that point either forward or backward. Alimentary canal. The esophagus, without glands and cilia (Fig. 2 C), opens into the ventral side of posterior rhynchodaeum. The stomach, which is about 1.3 – 2.8 mm in length, is divided into two regions.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:10360725",
          "authorship": "Liu & Sun",
          "yearPublished": "2018",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "b707818a-7bc3-5cb-839-ff81758e03e0a5"
        },
